<%- include('partials/header') %>

<link rel="stylesheet" href="/stylesheets/volunteer.css">

<main class="page-main-with-hero corporate-volunteering-main">
  <!-- Corporate Support reuses the Volunteer hero and content-card styling. -->
  <section class="page-hero-top corporate-volunteering-hero" aria-label="Corporate support page hero image">
    <img src="/images/2024/06/team-volunteering.jpg" alt="Corporate team supporting BKFA through a volunteering activity">
  </section>

  <div class="page-body-with-sidebar">
    <%- include('partials/getInvolvedSideMenu') %>

    <div class="page-content corporate-volunteering-page">
      <!-- Introduction and volunteering model. -->
      <section class="cv-intro">
        <h1>Corporate Support</h1>
        <h2>A High-Impact Employee Engagement Opportunity with Significant Social Outcomes</h2>

        <p>
          Birthing Kit Foundation Australia (BKFA) offers organisations a powerful way to activate their corporate social responsibility (CSR) and employee volunteering commitments while contributing to safer childbirth for women in vulnerable communities. Our volunteering model is practical, scalable, and designed to align with modern environmental, social, and governance (ESG), social impact, and employee volunteer engagement strategies.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="cv-intro">
        <h2>A Proven, Purpose-Driven Volunteering Experience</h2>

        <p>
          BKFA's Birthing Kit Assembly Days provide a structured, tangible hands-on volunteering activity that brings teams together to assemble clean birthing kits for distribution to global health partners at no cost in developing communities. These kits support safer, hygienic births in low-resource settings and directly contribute to improved maternal and newborn health outcomes.
        </p>

        <p><strong>Assembly Days are ideal for:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>Corporate volunteering programs</li>
          <li>Team-building and culture initiatives</li>
          <li>Environmental, social, and governance (ESG) and social impact activation</li>
          <li>Purpose-driven events that can be hosted in offices</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          BKFA supplies all materials, guidance, instructions, and support, ensuring a seamless experience for your organisation.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Business benefits and practical outcomes are separated for scanning. -->
      <section class="cv-details">
        <h2>Why Corporates Choose BKFA</h2>

        <p><strong>Key benefits for organisations include:</strong></p>
        <ul>
          <li>High-impact volunteering that directly supports global maternal health</li>
          <li>Strong alignment with Sustainable Development Goal (SDG) priorities, including SDG 3 (Good Health and Wellbeing), SDG 5 (Gender Equality), and SDG 12 (Responsible Consumption and Production)</li>
          <li>Engaging, inclusive activities suitable for teams of all sizes and abilities in most areas and countries</li>
          <li>Clear, tangible and easily explainable outcomes</li>
          <li>Positive employee experience, fostering teamwork, empathy, and purpose</li>
          <li>Flexible delivery: onsite, offsite, hybrid, or multi-location events</li>
        </ul>
      </section>

      <section class="cv-details">
        <h2>What Your Team Will Do</h2>

        <p>
          Volunteers assemble clean birthing kits containing six essential items: wrapped 12gm soap, 2 pairs of gloves, biodegradable plastic sheeting 1m x 1m, cord ties, a sterile size 22 scalpel blade, and gauze. These are placed in a biodegradable zip lock bag. These simple tools help reduce infection and complications during childbirth in low-resource environments.
        </p>

        <p>
          Each kit assembled by your team contributes directly to safer birthing conditions for women, girls, and newborns.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section class="cv-details">
        <h2>BKFA Provides Organisations With</h2>

        <ul>
          <li>Approved impact programs suitable for ESG, CSR, and annual reporting</li>
          <li>Metrics on kits assembled and communities supported</li>
          <li>Stories from the field through our global program partners</li>
          <li>Opportunities for ongoing partnership and engagement, including cross-marketing and media support</li>
        </ul>

        <p>
          Your organisation's contribution becomes part of a global effort to reduce preventable maternal and newborn deaths through education and the supply of Clean Birth Kits.
        </p>
      </section>

      <!-- Close with the partnership message used as the main call to action. -->
      <section class="cv-booking">
        <h2>Partner With BKFA</h2>
        <p>
          Corporate volunteering with BKFA is more than a one-day activity. It is a partnership that delivers purpose, impact, and connection. Together, our vision can be supported to help ensure women and girls have access to a clean and safe birth.
        </p>
        <p class="cv-tagline">
          Empower your teams. Strengthen your global conscience. Support safer births and gender equality worldwide.
        </p>
      </section>
    </div>
  </div>
</main>

<%- include('partials/footer') %>
